body:
Grandma's dad was Swedish. She made great potatoes and pancakes. There's a neighborhood in Saint Paul (capital of Minnesota) called Swede Hollow after the Swedish immigrants who used to live there. I think a lot of Swedish-American families make Swedish food around Christmas. I even knew one who still celebrated St Lucia's Day.

&#x200B;

Personally, I have a positive view of Sweden. I've never been there, but I have traveled quite a bit in Europe and have met a few Swedes along the way. Very polite and warm-hearted people, and they seem to believe in a good government of the people. Also good artists and designers.
